# LeakSanitizer suppressions for the sanitizer cell of CI
# (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=test/lsan.supp). A line suppresses every leak
# whose stack has a frame that matches the pattern.
#
# nginx allocates cycle->connections, cycle->read_events and
# cycle->write_events (and the smaller arrays of the event module) with
# ngx_alloc in ngx_event_process_init and never frees them: at exit it
# destroys the cycle pool and calls exit(). The three arrays point at each
# other (c->read, c->write, ev->data), so once nothing outside them points
# at them any more, LeakSanitizer reports all three as indirect leaks; when
# something still does, it reports nothing. The report therefore comes and
# goes with the platform and the run (seen on the x86-64 runner, not in the
# arm64 container). They are nginx's own allocations, so the report says
# nothing about ngx_mruby.
leak:^ngx_event_process_init$
